---
layout: page
title: Roadmap
description: The tickets in the epics labelled PrivateLandlord in the HDPI Jira project, with their status and dates, or a forecast where Jira has no dates yet.
---
{% include "data-notice.njk" %}
{% set s = roadmap.latest %}
{% if not s or not s.totals.epics %}
<p class="govuk-body">There are no epics labelled <code>PrivateLandlord</code> in HDPI yet. They will appear here the day after they are created.</p>
{% else %}
{% if roadmap.pdf %}<p class="govuk-body"><a class="govuk-link" href="/roadmap/roadmap.pdf" download>Download the A3 roadmap poster (PDF)</a></p>{% endif %}

<div class="app-chart">{{ roadmap.svg }}</div>
<p class="govuk-body-s">Each epic is followed by its tickets. Epic bars run from the epic's start date to its due date, and the dark part shows how many of its child items are done; a dashed epic bar means its dates come from its child items. Ticket bars are shaded by status: solid for done, mid-tone for in progress and pale for to do. A red outline marks a dependency clash.</p>
<div class="govuk-inset-text">Tickets drawn with a <strong>dashed outline and a paler fill</strong> are a <strong>forecast</strong>, not a plan. They have no start and due dates in Jira yet, so they are spread evenly, end to end and in ticket-number order, across the whole timeline ({{ s.start | date }} to {{ s.end | date }}). They will move to their real dates once those are set in Jira.</div>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Tickets</h2>
{% for r in roadmap.rows %}
<h3 class="govuk-heading-m"><a class="govuk-link" href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.key }}</a> {{ r.summary }}</h3>
<p class="govuk-body">{{ r.status | statusTag(r.category) }} {{ r.counts.done }} of {{ r.total }} items done.
{% if r.start %}Runs from {{ r.start | date }} to {{ r.due | date }}{% if r.derived %} (from its tickets' dates){% endif %}.{% else %}The epic has no dates in Jira.{% endif %}{% if s.lanes | length > 1 %} {{ r.lane }}.{% endif %}</p>
{% if r.items | length %}
<table class="govuk-table"><caption class="govuk-table__caption govuk-visually-hidden">Tickets in {{ r.key }}</caption>
<thead class="govuk-table__head"><tr class="govuk-table__row">
<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Ticket</th><th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Status</th>
<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Start</th><th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">End</th></tr></thead>
<tbody class="govuk-table__body">
{% for i in r.items %}<tr class="govuk-table__row">
<td class="govuk-table__cell"><a class="govuk-link app-nowrap" href="{{ i.url }}">{{ i.key }}</a> {{ i.summary }}</td>
<td class="govuk-table__cell">{{ i.status | statusTag(i.category) }}</td>
{% if i.forecast %}<td class="govuk-table__cell app-nowrap"><span class="app-forecast">Forecast</span><br>{{ i.start | date }}</td>
<td class="govuk-table__cell app-nowrap"><span class="app-forecast">Forecast</span><br>{{ i.due | date }}</td>
{% else %}<td class="govuk-table__cell app-nowrap">{{ i.start | date }}</td>
<td class="govuk-table__cell app-nowrap">{{ i.due | date }}</td>
{% endif %}</tr>
{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
{% if r.items | where("forecast", true) | length %}<p class="govuk-body-s">Forecast dates are not set in Jira. They are an even spread of the undated tickets across the timeline.</p>{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p class="govuk-body">No tickets are listed for this epic.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if s.clashes | length %}
<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Dependency clashes</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">These epics are set to start before the epic they depend on is due to finish.</p>
<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
{% for c in s.clashes %}<li>{{ c.after }} starts on {{ c.afterStart | date }}, but {{ c.before }} is not due until {{ c.beforeDue | date }}.</li>
{% endfor %}</ol>
{% endif %}

{% if s.totals.undated %}
<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Epics without dates</h2>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
{% for r in roadmap.rows %}{% if not r.start %}<li><a class="govuk-link" href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.key }}</a> {{ r.summary }}</li>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}

{% if roadmap.burnup %}
<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Burn-up</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">Child items across all epics: the dashed line is the total scope and the green line is the number done.</p>
<div class="app-chart">{{ roadmap.burnup }}</div>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
